"013:001 In that day they read in the book of Moses in the ears of the people; and it was found written in it, that the Ammonites and Moabites should not enter into the congregation of God for ever;",
"013:002 because they met not the children of Israel with bread and water, but hired Balaam against them to curse them: but our God turned the curse into a blessing.",
"013:003 And it came to pass, when they heard the law, that they were separated, even every alien in Israel.",
"013:004 And before this time Eliasib the priest lived in the treasury of the house of our God, connected with Tobias;",
"013:005 and he made himself a great treasury, and there they were formerly in the habit of bestowing the offerings, and the frankincense, and the vessels, and the tithe of the corn, and the wine, and the oil, the ordered portion of the Levites, and singers, and porters; and the first fruits of the priests.",
"013:006 But in all this time I was not in Jerusalem; for in the thirty-second year of Arthasastha king of Babylon I came to the king, and after a certain time I made my request of the king;",
"013:007 and I came to Jerusalem, and I understood the mischief which Eliasib had done in the case of Tobias, in making for him a treasury in the court of the house of God.",
"013:008 And it appeared very evil to me: so I cast forth all the furniture of the house of Tobias from the treasury.",
"013:009 And I gave orders, and they purified the treasuries: and I restored there the vessels of the house of God, and the offerings, and the frankincense.",
"013:010 And I understood that the portion of the Levites had not been given: and they had fled every one to his field, the Levites and the singers doing the work.",
"013:011 And I strove with the commanders, and said, Therefore has the house of God been abandoned? and I assembled them, and set them in their place.",
"013:012 And all Juda brought a tithe of the wheat and the wine and the oil into the treasuries,",
"013:013 to the charge of Selemia the priest, and Sadoc the scribe, and Phadaea of the Levites: and next to them was Anan the son of Zacchur, son of Matthanias; for they were accounted faithful: it was their office to distribute to their brethren.",
"013:014 Remember me, O God, in this, and let not my kindness be forgotten which I have wrought in regard to the house of the Lord God.",
"013:015 In those days I saw in Juda men treading wine presses on the sabbath, and carrying sheaves, and loading asses with both wine, and grapes, and figs, and every kind of burden, and bringing them into Jerusalem on the sabbath-day:",
"013:016 and I testified in the day of their sale. Also their lived in it men bringing fish, and selling every kind of merchandise to the children of Juda and in Jerusalem on the sabbath.",
"013:017 And I strove with the free children of Juda, and said to them, What is this evil thing which you do, and profane the sabbath-day?",
"013:018 Did not your fathers thus, and our God brought upon them and upon us and upon this city all these evils? and do you bring additional wrath upon Israel by profaning the sabbath?",
"013:019 And it came to pass, when the gates were set up in Jerusalem, before the sabbath, that I spoke, and they shut the gates; and I gave orders that they should not be opened till after the sabbath: and I set some of my servants at the gates, that none should bring in burdens on the sabbath-day.",
"013:020 So all the merchants lodged, and carried on traffic without Jerusalem once or twice.",
"013:021 Then I testified against them, and said to them, Why do you lodge in front of the wall? if you do so again, I will stretch out my hand upon you. From that time they came not on the sabbath.",
"013:022 and I told the Levites who were purifying themselves, and came and kept the gates, that they should sanctify the sabbath-day. Remember me, O God, for these things, and spare me according to the abundance of your mercy.",
"013:023 And in those days I saw the Jews who had married women of Ashdod, of Ammon, and of Moab:",
"013:024 and their children spoke half in the language of Ashdod, and did not know how to speak in the Jewish language.",
"013:025 And I strove with them and cursed them; and I struck some of them, and plucked off their hair, and made them swear by God, saying, You shall not give your daughters to their sons, and you shall not take of their daughters to your sons.",
"013:026 Did not Solomon king of Israel sin thus? though there was no king like him amongst many nations, and he was beloved of God, and God made him king over all Israel; yet strange women turned him aside.",
"013:027 So we will not listen to you to do all this evil, to break covenant with our God, —to marry strange wives.",
"013:028 and Elisub the high priest, one of the sons of Joada, being son-in-law of Sanaballat the Uranite, I chased him away from me.",
"013:029 Remember them, O God, for their false connection with the priesthood, and the breaking the covenant of the priesthood, and for defiling the Levites.",
"013:030 So I purged them from all foreign connection, and established courses for the priests and the Levites, every man according to his work.",
"013:031 And the offering of the wood-bearers was at certain set times, and in the times of the first fruits. Remember me, O our God, for good."
